  "result": "Perfect! All 120 tests pass. I've successfully implemented VAT calculations. Here's what was added:\n\n**New `lineVat(line)` function:**\n- Calculates VAT on the line amount **after discount** (not on the full line total)\n- Uses roundCents() for accurate monetary calculations\n- Formula: `(line total - line discount) \u00d7 vatRate / 100`\n\n**Modified `invoiceTotals` function:**\n- Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n- subtotal = sum of line totals\n- discount = sum of line discounts\n- vat = sum of line VATs (each calculated and rounded per line)\n- total = subtotal - discount + vat (clamped at 0, never negative)\n\n**Enhanced `renderInvoiceText` function:**\n- Shows VAT line (e.g., \"VAT: +\u20ac84.79\") when VAT > 0\n- VAT line appears just above the Total line\n- Uses formatEuros() for all amounts\n\n**Example output with VAT:**\n```\nDRAFT\nNorthwind Studio\n5 \u00d7 Design work (hour) @ \u20ac85.00 = \u20ac425.00 (5% off)\nSubtotal: \u20ac425.00\nDiscount: -\u20ac21.25\nVAT: +\u20ac84.79\nTotal: \u20ac488.54\n```\n\n**10 new tests** covering:\n- VAT at different rates (21%, 9%, 0%)\n- VAT on discounted amounts\n- Multiple lines with mixed VAT rates\n- VAT rendering in text output\n- Edge cases (100% discount with no VAT)\n\n**Updated all existing tests** to include VAT in calculations since total = subtotal - discount + vat.\n\nAll 120 tests pass. Request is complete.",
